            "body": "Heads-up: I think the functional half of this already landed, one day after you opened it.\n\n`#41275` ([Fix] deepseek-v4.1: Match KV capacity to physical layouts), merged 2026-10-27 as `20ff40cb8`, rewrites the same expression in the same place:\n\n```\n         if ratio in (1, 2):\n-            return (self.kv_bytes + self.low_ratio_index_bytes) / ratio\n+            return (\n+                self._get_paged_kv_bytes_per_token(ratio) + self.low_ratio_index_bytes\n+            ) / ratio\n```\n\nThe minus-line is byte-identical to yours; `#41275` just wrote it on three lines instead of one. Current `main` therefore already reads your version apart from the comment (python/sglang/srt/model_executor/pool_configurator.py, `_compressed_bytes_per_full_token`), so the only delta left in this patch is the two-line explanation.\n\nThat explanation is worth keeping on its own merits, because both numbers in it are right. Against `kernels/ops/attention/dsv4/kv_layout.py` on `main`: `V41_FP4` is `data_bytes` 256 + `scale_bytes` 32 = 288 bytes/token, and `V4` is 576 + 8 = 584 — the same 584 that `DeepSeekV4SingleKVPool.create_buffer` asserts as `448 + 64 * 2 + 8`. The old `self.kv_bytes` is also 584 (set to `qk_nope_head_dim + qk_rope_head_dim * 2 + 8`, commented \"One FlashMLA-layout latent slot\"), so an FP4 ratio-1/2 layer was budgeted at 584 for 288 bytes of real entry, about 2.03x, which is capacity the configurator gave up for bytes the pool never allocates. That is exactly the sort of regression a comment like this stops from coming back.\n\nSo the remaining choice is rebase-and-keep-as-comment-only, or close as superseded. If you rebase I will run it on 8xRTX PRO 5000 (SM120) with a DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash checkpoint and report the bytes-per-token the configurator ends up using for the ratio-1 and ratio-2 layers, before and after — it is doc-only, so I expect the same numbers, but I would rather confirm that than assume the rebase is clean.\n",
