    "body": "## Motivation\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1 keeps its ratio-1/2 compressed KV in `KVLayout.V41_FP4` (288 bytes an entry) on SM100, and on SM120 with #45851. The pool configurator still prices that entry at `kv_bytes`, which is the 584 bytes of a V4 FlashMLA slot, whatever layout the pool is built with.\n\nFor DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, which has kv_source layers 2, 8 and 14 at ratio 2 and layer 20 at ratio 1, the configurator therefore costs a full token at 1,630 bytes, but the pools allocate 890. The KV pool ends up holding about 55% of the tokens its memory budget covers.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`_compressed_bytes_per_full_token` now prices a ratio-1/2 entry with `_get_paged_kv_bytes_per_token(ratio)`, the entry size of the pool's own layout. The ratio-4 and ratio-128 pools are already priced this way. The indexer term is unchanged.\n\nLayouts that store 584 bytes an entry are unaffected. These are V4, the unified pools and trtllm, for which `_get_paged_kv_bytes_per_token` returns `kv_bytes` or the V4 page size.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThis changes only how many tokens the budget buys; the allocation and the kernels are unchanged.\n\nTest setup: DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 on one RTX 5070 Ti, SM120 with #45851, and the same 0.30 GB KV budget. With the larger pool the server serves normally:\n\n- the tool-call check passes 5/5;\n- the 24-piece mean NLL is 2.5965.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bytes_per_full_token` | 1,630 | 890 |\n| KV pool | 98,560 tokens | 180,480 tokens |\n| Free memory after the pool | 2.92 GB | 2.86 GB |\n\nFree memory after the pool is nearly unchanged, so the estimate now matches what the pools allocate.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit) (ruff format 0.15.1).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39884598185](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39884598185)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39884597882](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39884597882)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39884598194](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39884598194)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
